dict(pas="12.14", w="子張=zǐ zhāng/Zizhang | 問/asked about | 政。/government | ^子/the Master | 曰：「/said | ^居/dwelling (on) | 之/it | 無/without | 倦，/wearying | ^行=xíng/carrying (it) out | 之/(it) | 以/with | 忠。」/wholeheartedness",
  l="Zizhang asked about government.\nThe Master said: “Dwell on it without wearying;\ncarry it out with wholeheartedness.”",
  i="Zizhang asked about governing. The Master said: “Keep it in your mind and never tire of it; and in whatever you do in it, be wholehearted.”",
  n="Two matching clauses, verb + 之 'it' + how: 居之無倦 'dwell on it without wearying', 行之以忠 'carry it out with wholeheartedness'. 居 'to dwell, abide in'; 倦 'to weary'; 行 xíng 'to carry out'. Zhu Xi: 居 means keeping it in the heart — without wearying, beginning and end are one; 行 means putting it forth in affairs — with wholeheartedness, outside and inside are one. He quotes Master Cheng: Zizhang was short of humaneness; without a sincere heart that loves the people one is bound to tire and not give one's whole mind, so the Master told him this. He Yan's Wang Su: in the way of governing, hold it in one's own person without slackening, and carry it to the people always with wholeheartedness and good faith."),
