dict(pas="12.16", w="子/the Master | 曰：「/said | ^君子/the gentleman | 成/brings to completion | 人/others | 之/'s | 美，/fine (points) | ^不/does not | 成/bring to completion | 人/others | 之/'s | 惡。=è/bad (points) | ^小人/the small man | 反/reverses | 是。」/this",
  l="The Master said: “The gentleman completes what is fine in others;\nhe does not complete what is bad in others.\nThe small man reverses this.”",
  i="The Master said: “The gentleman helps the good in other people to its fulfilment and gives no help to the bad. With the small man it is the other way round.”",
  n="成 'to complete, bring about'; 美 'fine, beautiful' — here what is good in a man; 惡 è 'bad' (not wù 'to hate'). 人之美 / 人之惡: 之 is the genitive 'others' good / others' bad'. 反是 'reverses this', 是 'this' pointing back to the whole. Zhu Xi: 成 is to draw a man on, support him, encourage and reward him, so that his undertaking comes to completion; the gentleman and the small man differ in what they hold to, generous or mean, and in what they like, good or bad, and so the way they use their hearts differs like this."),
